From: Nelson Gill <ngill@slack-corp.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 09:53:32 -0700
Subject: fix: restore snap-compatible dbusmenu object path

The StatusNotifierItem multiplexer refactor in
https://crrev.com/c/8043132 changed the dbusmenu object path from
/com/canonical/dbusmenu to /org/chromium/DbusMenu.

Under snap strict confinement the unity7 interface grants dbusmenu
access only on the /com/canonical/dbusmenu path. Traffic on
/org/chromium/DbusMenu is silently dropped by AppArmor, so the
desktop environment panel never receives the menu layout and the tray
context menu is non-functional for every snap-confined application.

The bus name half of this problem was already fixed upstream in
https://crrev.com/c/8337991. This patch fixes the remaining dbusmenu
path half.

/com/canonical/dbusmenu is the conventional path used by libdbusmenu
and expected by all StatusNotifierWatcher implementations. The SNI
specification does not mandate a specific dbusmenu object path, so
either works outside of snap confinement.

This patch can be removed once snapd ships support for the new path
(https://github.com/canonical/snapd/pull/17415) and sufficient
adoption time has passed.

Upstream snapd bug: https://bugs.launchpad.net/snapd/+bug/2161950

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/views/status_icons/status_icon_linux_dbus.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/views/status_icons/status_icon_linux_dbus.cc
index 756f5127309519a8049afadb58db60447bd5dfe8..921472e161f7766000e1c1f60ed043258d268e86 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/status_icons/status_icon_linux_dbus.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/status_icons/status_icon_linux_dbus.cc
@@ -72,7 +72,7 @@ const char kInterfaceStatusNotifierWatcher[] = "org.kde.StatusNotifierWatcher";
 // Object paths.
 const char kPathStatusNotifierItem[] = "/StatusNotifierItem";
 const char kPathStatusNotifierWatcher[] = "/StatusNotifierWatcher";
-const char kPathDbusMenu[] = "/org/chromium/DbusMenu";
+const char kPathDbusMenu[] = "/com/canonical/dbusmenu";
 
 // Methods.
 const char kMethodNameHasOwner[] = "NameHasOwner";
